  "claim": "22 September 1791 is the birth date of this English scientist. His laboratory burner design was later perfected by another scientist, forming the device of which the Teclu burner is a hotter-flamed variant. This other scientist was the laboratory assistant of Robert Bunsen.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Peter Desaga. Sentence: Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\nPage: Peter Desaga. Sentence: In 1855, Desaga perfected an earlier design of the laboratory burner by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\nPage: Michael Faraday. Sentence: Michael Faraday FRS ( ; 22 September 1791 – 25 August 1867) was an English scientist who contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\nPage: Robert Bunsen. Sentence: With his laboratory assistant, Peter Desaga, he developed the Bunsen burner, an improvement on the laboratory burners then in use.\nPage: Teclu burner. Sentence: The Teclu burner is a laboratory gas burner, a variant of the Bunsen burner, named after the Romanian chemist Nicolae Teclu.",
